  "final_message": "I haven't removed anything yet, because the `channel` field on `OrderPlaced` is still read downstream.\n\n`analytics-ingest` requires it:\n- `analytics-ingest/src/core/events.ts:34` parses `channel` with `reader.oneOf(\"channel\", CHANNELS)`.\n- Its README says a missing or unknown `channel` makes ingestion reject the whole event with a `ContractViolationError`.\n- `analytics-ingest/src/ingest.ts:17` writes it to the `channel` column of the `orders` table.\n- Its test `requires channel` expects a missing `channel` to be rejected.\n\nIf orders-service stopped publishing `channel`, every `OrderPlaced` event would be rejected by analytics-ingest. That repo is read-only for me and belongs to another team.\n\n`billing-service` only uses `channel` in its test fixtures. Its test at `onOrderPlaced.test.ts:106` passes `channel: undefined`, so it probably tolerates the field being gone.\n\nWhich of these do you want?\n1. **Remove it from the order model only.** The event would keep `channel`, which means giving it a fixed value or carrying it some other way. That's awkward.\n2. **Remove it from both, as you asked.** analytics-ingest would need to drop the requirement first or at the same time, so this depends on that team.\n3. **Wait** until analytics-ingest has stopped requiring it, then do the full removal.\n\nIf you pick option 2 or 3, I'll update these places in orders-service:\n- `src/core/order.ts`\n- `src/core/events.ts`\n- `src/api/requestParsing.ts`\n- the tests\n- the examples in `README.md` and `CLAUDE.md`\n\nI'd also remove the `channel` validation path and the `CHANNELS` constant.",
